                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "gxdMG",
                      "name": "note",
                      "fill": "$ink-muted",
                      "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                      "width": "fill_container",
                      "content": "the set viewer's pinned bar, one line above 768px and stacked below it: tier badges, a theme strip, a viewport strip and a count of what is showing. The shell header pins above it — scoped to this page, so packages/ui keeps its refusal and its baselines. Native radios styled as one connected strip, NOT the SegmentedControl atom, which is a client button group needing onChange; :checked drives visibility through :has(), so the page keeps zero client JavaScript. The tier badge you JUMPED to is marked by :target — it answers a click and survives a reload, and does not follow free scrolling, because no selector can observe that. A story a filter empties is hidden, never left as an empty card.",
                      "lineHeight": 1.4,
                      "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                      "fontSize": 11,
                      "fontWeight": "normal"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
